// The multi-output PICKER page - the sneak+F selection surface for a station whose placed
// input matches recipes across multiple native categories at once. A vertical RECIPE LIST:
// one full-width card per available output category, appended from RpgStationPickerPage.build
// via RpgStationPickerTab.ui. Never auto-opened; opened only on sneak+F when a station's input
// matches recipes across multiple native categories.
//
// THE BAND: the page sits on CommonLib's band frame (@ZigDecoratedFrame), which blurs and dims the
// world and draws the game's modal band across the screen, its head and foot reaching 78 above and
// below this page's box. So the box has a fixed height, set from Java on #RpgStationPickerRoot's
// Anchor (PickerCategories.boxHeight: the title, the hint and the cards, the list capped so the
// tallest box and its band fit a 1080 screen; past the cap the list scrolls). The heights below are
// the numbers PickerCategories adds up, and RpgStationPickerPageTest holds the two together. The
// Height written here is the box for two cards with their cost lines, the fewest the picker opens
// with; build always sets the real one.
//
// COMPACT PANEL: a page's document root force-stretches to fill the viewport, so the sized box
// (#RpgStationPickerRoot) must NOT be this document's directly-appended root. It is wrapped in the
// native $C.@PageOverlay (full-viewport dim, intentional) with LayoutMode: Middle, which CENTERS its
// child instead of stretching it (the vanilla small-dialog pattern of PrefabEditorExitConfirm.ui and
// NameRespawnPointPage.ui).
//
// Every colour and size is CommonLib's (the title the frame's title label, the hint the kit's body
// text). Document path + top-level ids are mod-namespaced (RpgStationPicker.ui / #RpgStationPicker*) so
// a co-installed mod's page cannot clobber this one on the client's flat namespace.

$C = "../Common.ui";
$F = "../Common/ZigFrames.ui";
$ZX = "../Common/ZigText.ui";

$C.@PageOverlay {
  LayoutMode: Middle;

  Group #RpgStationPickerRoot {
    Anchor: (Width: 640, Height: 346);

    $F.@ZigDecoratedFrame {
      @CloseButton = true;
      Anchor: (Width: 640);

      #Content {
        Label #RpgStationPickerTitle {
          Text: "";
          Anchor: (Height: 30);
          Style: (...$F.@ZigTitleLabelStyle, HorizontalAlignment: Center);
        }

        // Two lines at most in the column's whole width, so a longer translation wraps once.
        Label #RpgStationPickerHint {
          Text: "";
          Anchor: (Top: 4, Height: 40);
          Style: (...$ZX.@ZigBodyStyle, HorizontalAlignment: Center, Wrap: true, WrapMaxLines: 2);
        }

        // The recipe list - one full-width card per output category, appended here from
        // RpgStationPickerPage#build via RpgStationPickerTab.ui. TopScrolling stacks them vertically
        // (each card carries its own Anchor.Bottom gap) and scrolls once they outgrow the box; the
        // right padding is the scrollbar's room, which the cards' width leaves.
        Group #RpgStationPickerTabs {
          Anchor: (Top: 16);
          FlexWeight: 1;
          LayoutMode: TopScrolling;
          ScrollbarStyle: $C.@DefaultScrollbarStyle;
          Padding: (Right: 8);
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
